    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[William Henry Haines (Wikipedia — did you know?)]]></title>
        <id>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Henry_Haines</id>
        <link href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Henry_Haines"/>
        <updated>2026-10-19T11:05:08.112Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[... that paintings of Venice by <b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/William_Henry_Haines" title="William Henry Haines">William Henry Haines</a></b> <i>(example pictured)</i> were passed off as the work of old Italian masters like <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Canaletto" title="Canaletto">Canaletto</a>?]]></content>
    </entry>
    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Mount Bonaparte (Wikipedia — did you know?)]]></title>
        <id>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Bonaparte</id>
        <link href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Bonaparte"/>
        <updated>2026-10-19T11:05:08.125Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[... that the 7,257-foot (2,212<span typeof="mw:Entity">&nbsp;</span>m) <b><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Bonaparte" title="Mount Bonaparte">Mount Bonaparte</a></b> had a cistern hand-carved into its granite summit in 1929?]]></content>
    </entry>
    <entry>
